{
  "schema_version": 3,
  "name": "Feature showcase",
  "description": "A teaching demo that exercises every widget and the most important features of the ScripTree schema, written for people who have never touched a .scriptree file before.\n\nThe target tool is PowerShell's Get-ChildItem (the modern replacement for `dir` / `ls` on Windows). Every Windows machine already has PowerShell, so nothing needs to be installed to run this form. The form's job is to teach you how the schema works — the underlying command is just an excuse to wire up real fields.\n\nWhat to look for as you click through:\n  - 'Mode' (Browse tab) is a RADIO group. Changing it shows/hides downstream fields via visible_when.\n  - 'Preset filter' (Browse tab) is a DROPDOWN whose choices are 'preset bundles' — one choice can carry a multi-token filter expression.\n  - 'Preview file' (Browse tab) is a DROPDOWN whose choices come from an external script run when the form opens (choices_provider). Pick a target directory above it and click the Refresh button (the small circular arrow on the field) to repopulate.\n  - 'Columns to show' (Output tab) is a CHECKBOX_LIST with a select-all/none master — each tick repeats the property name as a Select-Object argument.\n  - 'Search folders' (Output tab) is a FOLDER_LIST: an ordered list with Add / Remove / Up / Down. Drop folders onto it from Explorer.\n  - 'Reference files' (Output tab) is a FILE_LIST, the file equivalent of folder_list.\n  - 'Destructive-action checkbox' (Safety tab) shows the convention real tools use for destructive operations: a clearly-named, unticked-by-default boolean. Pair with `required_when` to block Run until the user opts in.\n  - The 'Cell appearance' section of this file (open the .scriptree in a text editor) embeds a PNG icon and sets a fill colour so the launcher cell shows a coloured hex with a gear glyph.\n  - Every other field has an in-form description aimed at a beginner. Hover any field's label to see it again as a tooltip.\n\nDrag-and-drop reminder: every text / file / save_file / folder / textarea / folder_list / file_list widget accepts file or folder drops from Explorer. Try dragging the demo folder onto 'Target directory' below.\n\nCanonical docs (read these next):\n  D:\\Dev\\ScripTree\\help\\LLM\\param_types_widgets.md\n  D:\\Dev\\ScripTree\\help\\LLM\\argument_template.md\n  D:\\Dev\\ScripTree\\help\\LLM\\dynamic_providers.md",
  "executable": "powershell",
  "working_directory": ".",
  "sections": [
    {
      "name": "Browse",
      "layout": "tab"
    },
    {
      "name": "Output",
      "layout": "tab"
    },
    {
      "name": "Safety",
      "layout": "tab"
    },
    {
      "name": "About this demo",
      "layout": "tab"
    }
  ],
  "argument_template": [
    "-NoLogo",
    "-NoProfile",
    "-NonInteractive",
    "-Command",
    "Get-ChildItem",
    "-Path",
    "{target_dir}",
    "{include_hidden?-Force}",
    "{recursive?-Recurse}",
    [
      "-Depth",
      "{max_depth}"
    ],
    [
      "-Filter",
      "{name_filter}"
    ],
    "{preset_filter}",
    [
      "-Include",
      "{reference_files}"
    ],
    [
      "-LiteralPath",
      "{search_folders}"
    ],
    "|",
    "Select-Object",
    "{columns}",
    "|",
    "Format-Table",
    "-AutoSize"
  ],
  "params": [
    {
      "id": "mode",
      "label": "Mode",
      "description": "Pick what kind of listing you want. This is a RADIO group: only one option can be selected at a time, and the other fields on this tab adjust to match.\n\n  - Browse one folder: list a single directory you pick.\n  - Compare folders: list ordered folders (uses the 'Search folders' list on the Output tab).\n  - Inspect single file: preview one file picked from the dynamic dropdown below.\n\nThe field types radio / checkbox_list / folder_list / file_list each render as a distinct Qt widget; see param_types_widgets.md for the full type × widget compatibility matrix.",
      "type": "enum",
      "widget": "radio",
      "required": true,
      "default": "browse",
      "choices": [
        "browse",
        "compare",
        "inspect"
      ],
      "choice_labels": [
        "Browse one folder",
        "Compare folders (uses 'Search folders' list)",
        "Inspect single file (uses dynamic dropdown)"
      ],
      "section": "Browse"
    },
    {
      "id": "target_dir",
      "label": "Target directory",
      "description": "The folder Get-ChildItem will list. You can:\n  - Click Browse and pick a folder.\n  - Type a path, e.g. C:\\Windows or %USERPROFILE%.\n  - Drag a folder from Explorer onto this field (drag-and-drop is built into every text / file / folder widget).\n\nThis path is also forwarded to the dynamic dropdown below as an upstream dependency (see depends_on).",
      "type": "path",
      "widget": "folder",
      "required": true,
      "default": ".",
      "section": "Browse",
      "visible_when": "mode == 'browse'"
    },
    {
      "id": "name_filter",
      "label": "Name filter (-Filter)",
      "description": "Wildcard pattern applied by the filesystem driver. Examples:\n  *.txt     all text files\n  log-*     anything beginning with log-\n  *.{md,rst}  (PowerShell does NOT expand this — use 'Preset filter' below for that)\n\nLeave blank to list everything in the folder.",
      "type": "string",
      "widget": "text",
      "required": false,
      "default": "",
      "section": "Browse",
      "visible_when": "mode == 'browse' OR mode == 'compare'"
    },
    {
      "id": "preset_filter",
      "label": "Preset filter (dropdown of bundled expressions)",
      "description": "A DROPDOWN whose choices are 'preset bundles' — the canonical highest-leverage pattern in the schema. Each choice is a single string that gets passed to PowerShell verbatim, but the string can carry an entire pipeline fragment. Compare with the trivial 'auto / always / never' enums you see in fd or eza: those are one token each. These are several tokens each.\n\nPick a preset; the form's command-preview at the bottom of the runner will show how the choice expands. Pick '(none)' to emit nothing.\n\nRecipe in param_types_widgets.md § 'Preset bundles — the highest-leverage enum pattern'. When you wrap a CLI with rich filter syntax, prefer 15-25 bundled presets over a free-form text field.",
      "type": "enum",
      "widget": "dropdown",
      "required": false,
      "default": "",
      "choices": [
        "",
        "| Where-Object { $_.Length -gt 1MB }",
        "| Where-Object { $_.LastWriteTime -gt (Get-Date).AddDays(-7) }",
        "| Where-Object { -not $_.PSIsContainer }",
        "| Where-Object { $_.PSIsContainer }",
        "| Where-Object { $_.Name -match '\\.(md|rst|txt)$' }",
        "| Sort-Object Length -Descending | Select-Object -First 10"
      ],
      "choice_labels": [
        "(none) — emit nothing",
        "Larger than 1 MB",
        "Modified in the last 7 days",
        "Files only (skip subfolders)",
        "Folders only",
        "Markdown / RST / TXT only",
        "Top 10 largest"
      ],
      "section": "Browse"
    },
    {
      "id": "preview_file",
      "label": "Preview file (dynamic dropdown, populated at form-open)",
      "description": "This DROPDOWN's choices are NOT baked into the .scriptree. ScripTree runs the sibling script `list_files.py` at form-open time and reads a JSON document from its stdout (the contract is in dynamic_providers.md). The script lists files in the 'Target directory' above; change that field and click the small refresh button beside this dropdown to repopulate.\n\nWhen would you actually use a provider in real life? When the choices only exist at form-open time — currently-open drawings in SolidWorks, running Docker containers, git remotes, database tables, etc. For tools whose choices ARE knowable at authoring time, a plain static `choices` list is simpler and faster.",
      "type": "enum",
      "widget": "dropdown",
      "required": false,
      "default": "",
      "section": "Browse",
      "visible_when": "mode == 'inspect'",
      "depends_on": [
        "target_dir"
      ],
      "choices_provider": {
        "command": [
          "python",
          "./list_files.py"
        ],
        "working_directory": ".",
        "refresh": "on_change",
        "timeout_sec": 10,
        "cache": "form_session"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "recursive",
      "label": "Recurse into subfolders (-Recurse)",
      "description": "Walk subdirectories. Off by default. Used when 'Mode' is 'Browse one folder' or 'Compare folders'.",
      "type": "boolean",
      "widget": "checkbox",
      "required": false,
      "default": false,
      "section": "Browse",
      "visible_when": "mode == 'browse' OR mode == 'compare'"
    },
    {
      "id": "include_hidden",
      "label": "Include hidden / system items (-Force)",
      "description": "Show items whose hidden or system bit is set. Off by default.",
      "type": "boolean",
      "widget": "checkbox",
      "required": false,
      "default": false,
      "section": "Browse"
    },
    {
      "id": "max_depth",
      "label": "Max recursion depth (-Depth)",
      "description": "Cap how many subfolder levels Get-ChildItem will descend when recursing. 0 = unlimited (default), 1 = current folder only, 2 = one level deep, etc. The min / max / step fields on this param are honoured by the spin-box widget — try clicking the up/down arrows or pressing Page Up / Page Down. See param_types_widgets.md § 'number' for the bounds.",
      "type": "integer",
      "widget": "number",
      "required": false,
      "default": 0,
      "min": 0,
      "max": 25,
      "step": 1,
      "section": "Browse",
      "visible_when": "recursive == 'true'"
    },
    {
      "id": "columns",
      "label": "Columns to show (multiselect / checkbox_list)",
      "description": "A CHECKBOX_LIST: a scrollable column of checkboxes with a select-all/none master at the top (the `select_all: true` field). Each ticked entry is forwarded to PowerShell's Select-Object as one property name. Run the form to see the columns assemble into the output table.\n\nUnder the hood, the placeholder for this field is embedded in the bare token '{columns}'. ScripTree comma-joins a multiselect's values when the placeholder sits alone (or is embedded in a literal); it FANS OUT (one repeat per element) when the placeholder is the only bare entry in a list-form token group. See argument_template.md §5.",
      "type": "multiselect",
      "widget": "checkbox_list",
      "select_all": true,
      "required": false,
      "default": [
        "Name",
        "Length",
        "LastWriteTime"
      ],
      "choices": [
        "Name",
        "FullName",
        "Length",
        "LastWriteTime",
        "CreationTime",
        "Attributes",
        "Extension",
        "Mode",
        "PSIsContainer",
        "DirectoryName"
      ],
      "choice_labels": [
        "Name (file/folder name)",
        "FullName (full path)",
        "Length (size in bytes)",
        "LastWriteTime (modified date)",
        "CreationTime (created date)",
        "Attributes (hidden / readonly / archive)",
        "Extension (.txt, .md, ...)",
        "Mode (-a---- style flags)",
        "PSIsContainer (true for folders)",
        "DirectoryName (parent folder)"
      ],
      "section": "Output"
    },
    {
      "id": "search_folders",
      "label": "Search folders (folder_list, multi-path picker)",
      "description": "An ordered FOLDER_LIST: paths are composed by clicking Add (opens a folder picker), or by dragging folders from Explorer onto the list. Reorder with the Up / Down buttons. The min_items field below makes the form require at least one entry when 'Mode' is 'Compare folders'; the must_exist flag stops users from adding folders that aren't on disk right now.\n\nIn the argv template this field sits inside the token group [\"-LiteralPath\", \"{search_folders}\"]. Because of the token-group fan-out rule, three folders selected produce '-LiteralPath A -LiteralPath B -LiteralPath C' (NOT a single comma-joined token). See argument_template.md §5.",
      "type": "multiselect",
      "widget": "folder_list",
      "required": false,
      "default": [],
      "must_exist": true,
      "min_items": 0,
      "section": "Output"
    },
    {
      "id": "reference_files",
      "label": "Reference files (file_list, multi-file picker)",
      "description": "A FILE_LIST: same Add/Remove/Up/Down shell as folder_list but the picker is a file-open dialog. The file_filter field below restricts the Add dialog to text-like files; users can still drop other files onto the list directly.\n\nFanned out into '-Include FILE -Include FILE -Include FILE' via the token group in the argument template.",
      "type": "multiselect",
      "widget": "file_list",
      "required": false,
      "default": [],
      "file_filter": "Text-like files (*.txt *.md *.rst *.log);;All files (*)",
      "must_exist": false,
      "section": "Output"
    },
    {
      "id": "destructive_intent",
      "label": "Destructive-action checkbox (just a label)",
      "description": "Real production tools that delete files, overwrite outputs, or push to remotes should make the destructive intent explicit in the form. A common pattern is to add a checkbox like 'Yes, I want to <do the irreversible thing>' that is unticked by default and clearly named. Combine with a `required_when` expression so Run is blocked until the user opts in.\n\nThis checkbox is wired into the argv as a boolean — toggle it and watch the live command preview to see -ConfirmAction appear / disappear (the flag is fictitious for Get-ChildItem; it's here to show the wiring).",
      "type": "boolean",
      "widget": "checkbox",
      "required": false,
      "default": false,
      "section": "Safety"
    },
    {
      "id": "dry_run_note",
      "label": "Verbose output (a textarea you can drag files onto)",
      "description": "A TEXTAREA widget — the multi-line cousin of 'text'. Drop one or more files from Explorer onto it; each dropped path is inserted at the cursor on its own line. Useful when you want users to paste in a list of paths or a long regex without the field clipping.\n\nThe textarea content is currently NOT wired into the argv (this field is just a demo of the widget). Try typing or dropping anyway.",
      "type": "string",
      "widget": "textarea",
      "required": false,
      "default": "Notes / scratch space — drag files from Explorer onto this textarea to see drop-handling in action.",
      "section": "Safety"
    },
    {
      "id": "demo_url",
      "label": "Where to learn more",
      "description": "Paste a URL or path here. Demonstrates the masking heuristic from param_types_widgets.md § 'text with masking': labels containing 'password' / 'secret' / 'token' / 'api key' automatically render with QLineEdit.Password echo mode — try changing this field's label to 'API key' in the .scriptree to see the dots appear.",
      "type": "string",
      "widget": "text",
      "required": false,
      "default": "https://github.com/KenM76/scriptree-demos",
      "section": "About this demo"
    },
    {
      "id": "demo_save_target",
      "label": "Save the output to (save_file widget)",
      "description": "A SAVE_FILE picker. Same as 'file' but the Browse button opens the system Save-As dialog so users pick a destination that doesn't exist yet. The field is not wired into this form's argv; redirect the runner's output to disk yourself if you want it captured.",
      "type": "path",
      "widget": "save_file",
      "required": false,
      "default": "",
      "file_filter": "Plain text (*.txt);;Markdown (*.md);;All files (*)",
      "section": "About this demo"
    }
  ],
  "cell": {
    "icon_data": "",
    "icon_format": "png",
    "fill_color": "#4C6FBF",
    "text_label": "FX",
    "text_color": "#FFFFFF"
  },
  "source": {
    "mode": "manual",
    "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/module/microsoft.powershell.management/get-childitem"
  }
}
